      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "व्यतिरेकः स एव सः । There is व्य० when the superiority over the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "उपमान ( the standard of comparison ) of what is different from",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "it is mentioned, as that of सतां प्रज्ञोन्मेष over भू &c., here.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 11. The idea of the sl. is that one should make once",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "for all a choice of the alternatives stated and act accordingly;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "भार्या—भ्रियते इति भार्याः fr. भृ+य ( ण्यत्, ) भर्तुं योग्या वा; he should",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "have the one or the other and nothing between these.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 12. कमठ—के जले मठति इति; aff. अ ( अच् ); a tortoise. Here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the great Tortoise—Vishnu’s कूर्मावतार. कुलाचल—Name of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "seven principal mountain chains, for which see com. दिग्गज—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "The elephants of the quarters, supporting and guarding them.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "The names are thus given by Amarasimha-ऐरावतः पुण्डरीको वामनः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "कुमुदोञ्जनः ॥ पुष्पदन्तः सार्वभौमः सुप्रतीकश्च दिग्गजाः ॥ The Ràmàyana",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "gives them differently, viz. Virupâksha for the East, Saumanasa",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "for the West, Mahâpadma for the South, and Bhadra for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "the North.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "प्रतिपन्न-what is undertaken. अमलमनसाम्-of those whose minds",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "are pure, i. e. who never use equivocal language but state in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "unmistakable terms what they would do. It is not clear what",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the gist of the sl. is. The connection between strong-mind-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "edness and amalamanasatva is not very clear. Probably the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "poet expresses here the same idea as he does in the last line",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of the next sloka. The fig. is व्यतिरेक,",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 12. कूर्मस्य—कौ जले ऊर्मिः वेगो अस्य । A tortoise. Here the se-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "cond incarnation of Vishnu. Mr. Telang reads the third line as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "किं त्वङ्गी०—न्न मनसा, suggesting that the line should be taken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "as a question and that for this it would be better to read किं चा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ङ्गीकृतम्, and further remarks—“The reading किंतु is more appro-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "priate to what I think is the intended sense, but to obtain that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "न must be got rid of.” But the third line makes a general",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "statement and supports the figure in the last line, while the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "questions in the first two lines refer to specifie objects. निर्वाहः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "&c.—construe सतामेतद्धि गोत्रव्रतं ( यत् ) प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु निर्वाहः । व्रत—",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
